  "published": "2026-05-10T21:12:25.73Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.0:\n- Add IRequestExceptionHandler<TRequest, TResponse, TException> (MediatR-compatible). Implementations may recover from exceptions thrown by the handler or any pipeline step by calling RequestExceptionHandlerState.SetHandled with a fallback response. Multiple handlers per (request, exception) pair are supported and run in registration order until one marks the state as handled. Matches by exception type assignability so a handler for a base type catches derived exceptions.\n- Add IRequestExceptionAction<TRequest, TException> (MediatR-compatible). Side-effects (logging, metrics, ...) triggered by an exception that has not been recovered. The original exception is always re-thrown after all matching actions complete; actions are skipped when an exception handler recovers via SetHandled.\n- Add explicit registration via cfg.AddRequestExceptionHandler<T>() and cfg.AddRequestExceptionAction<T>(); the wrapper pipeline behaviors are wired automatically.\n- Exception handlers and actions are auto-scanned from assemblies unconditionally (no opt-in flag), mirroring MediatR.",
